[ti:Before the Fade]
[00:02.92][Intro]
[00:03.00]Midnight hums in shades of blue
[00:08.28]A map unwritten, waiting to be drawn anew
[00:30.44][Verse]
[00:30.52]I walk where the streetlight loses its name
[00:34.36]Learning the language of a different rain
[00:37.80]Each wrong turn leaves a mark on my sleeve
[00:41.84]Proof of the roads I was scared to believe
[00:45.20]The horizon moves, so I move with it too
[00:48.88]Past all the rules that never came true
[00:52.20]I wear the unknown like a second skin
[00:55.12]Keeping one small match alive in the wind
[00:59.72]Still I rise before the fade
[01:03.40]Still I chase the light I made
[01:06.40]Out on the edge where tomorrow waits
[01:10.56]I'm becoming what tomorrow makes
[01:29.64][Verse]
[01:29.72]Deep in the fog, I found a steadier hand
[01:33.16]Every river redrew where I stand
[01:36.40]I keep small hours like coins in my coat
[01:39.68]Warm from the crossing, enough to stay afloat
[01:43.32]They watched from the shore while I learned to swim
[01:47.04]Now even the tide has changed its hymn
[01:50.72]Softer than thunder, clear as the glass
[01:53.96]I build what will stay when the old days pass
[01:58.80]Still I rise before the fade
[02:02.48]Still I chase the light I made
[02:05.48]Out on the edge where tomorrow waits
[02:09.64]I'm becoming what tomorrow makes
[02:28.92][Bridge]
[02:29.00]I thought the map had to tell me where
[02:32.24]But dawn found my footprints already there
[02:35.92]No finish line, no hand to hold
[02:39.60]Just my own fire against the cold
[02:46.68][Refrain]
[02:46.76]Still I rise before the fade
[02:50.44]Still I chase the light I made
[02:53.44]Out on the edge where tomorrow waits
[02:57.56]I'm becoming what tomorrow makes
